## Skills to use

When work affects planning, PR evidence, demos, or publication docs, invoke the `tusker` skill.

## Workflow expectations

- The task note is the unit of work. Agent capsule, intent, acceptance, deliverables, verification, and evidence are sections inside it.
- Use `tusker search` and exact task paths before broad repository search when looking for existing tracker work.
- Use `tusker list --type epic` first; drill into one epic with `tusker list --epic <ACR> --type task --open`.
- Use `tusker compact <ID>` as a dry-run before reading or editing old noisy task notes.
- Keep lookup and bookkeeping updates light; do not run closeout ceremony unless moving implementation work to review/done.
- Keep the contract sections stable. Put durable truth in the capsule, evidence summary, verification summary, close summary, and knowledge delta.
- Create a user doc or developer doc when the work changes external behavior or operator-facing surfaces.
- Reindex and validate the vault after material updates.
- Do not load `tusker/Attachments/**`, generated indexes, raw runner logs, or full build logs unless the task specifically requires evidence forensics.
